The meshes in this folder are converted from the cf21B STL files of Crazyflow
(https://github.com/learnsyslab/crazyflow, formerly utiasDSL/crazyflow, commit
c95f69bc54f830e859fee4ac5734bf571acd81f3, folder crazyflow/drones/assets/cf21B):

  body.glb      cf21B_pcb, cf21B_motors, cf21B_prop-guards, cf21B_connectors, cf21B_connector-pins,
                cf21B_battery and cf21B_battery-holder, one node each
  prop_ccw.glb  cf21B_PropL
  prop_cw.glb   cf21B_PropR

placed and coloured as Crazyflow's crazyflow/drones/cf21B_500.xml places and colours them. Changes made here:
scaled from millimetres to metres, vertices closer than 1 micrometre merged, shaded smooth below 30 degrees,
the MJCF colours converted from sRGB to linear values, a roughness of 0.5 chosen. The geometry is otherwise
unchanged, and its frame is the source's (x forward, y left, z up, origin at the centre of the four motor axes
in the circuit-board plane).

Licence. Crazyflow's repository is distributed under the MIT License, reproduced below, and packages these
files under it. Whether the files are Crazyflow's to license is not established:

  - The STL files carry an Autodesk export header and name no author, and no public CAD source of them is
    known.
  - In the same Crazyflow folder, cf_led-diffuser.stl (not used here) is byte-identical to led-diffuser.stl in
    Bitcraze's bitcraze-mechanics repository (https://github.com/bitcraze/bitcraze-mechanics, commit
    d9f18d7147d66fb2a8c53775ef9d5761e6536e78), which Bitcraze licenses under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0.
  - The propeller guards, cf21B_prop-guards.stl, lie on the surface of Bitcraze's
    models/CF21-BL_guards_v1_40k_vertices.stl from that repository, in the same frame, to within 0.003 mm for
    95 % of their vertices: it is the same guard geometry, tessellated differently.
  - The circuit board, motors, propellers, connectors and battery holder have no counterpart in that
    repository.

